---
import Figure from "../Figure.astro";
---
<Figure width="wide">
  <ol class="steps-row" style="--n:3">
    <li><b>Cold · from step one</b>Simple bandit rules choose the edit type, the parent and when to refine, from recent rewards alone, keeping every option in play. Nothing is known yet, so nothing is assumed.</li>
    <li class="w"><b>Warm · after a few dozen steps</b>The world model joins: it forecasts which steps will pay and screens the rest, but only while it beats the simple estimates on steps it was not trained on.</li>
    <li><b>Hot · after a few hundred steps, or inherited</b>A policy trained by reinforcement learning on the whole population's logged decisions. A run that inherits steps and a policy from an earlier run starts here.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="chart" id="ladder" style="margin-top:28px"></div>
  <div class="legend"><span><i style="background:var(--fig-rule-strong)"></i>bandits plan the step</span><span><i style="background:#3A6EA5"></i>world model plans</span><span><i style="background:#3F8F5C"></i>RL policy plans</span><span><i class="ln" style="background:#3A6EA5"></i>world-model error</span><span><i class="ln" style="background:var(--fig-muted)"></i>simple estimate</span></div>
  <Fragment slot="caption">
    <b>Control passes on only when it is earned.</b> Top: who planned each step of this run. Bottom: the world model's
    forecast error at each refit against the best simple estimate (lower is better). A filled marker means it passed
    the check and steers; a hollow one means it was held back.
  </Fragment>
</Figure>
